{
 "kind": "sqll-s3-sqruff-tree-handcheck",
 "format": 1,
 "method": "The author of the classifier checked each case. For each case: read the output of 'sqruff_trees.py show ID' (another method than the classifier: the change of the ancestor types of each leaf), and where it was not clear, the unified diff of the 2 trees and the hunks. Then write the classes that the class definitions give. Limits: the checker also wrote the classifier, thus the check is not independent. The first check found hunks next to unparsable nodes that follow from the parse failure (for example impala/null_safe_equal and snowflake/create_stream gave nesting and wrapper hunks). The unparsable region rule and the meta key changed after that. The sample was selected again and checked on the final classifier.",
